🔹 Program 7: Friend / Non-Member Operator Overloading

📌 Description

This program demonstrates operator overloading using a friend non-member function.

It allows an integer to appear on the left side of the "+" operator:

"10 + number"

A friend function is used because the left operand is an integer rather than a "Complex" object.

🎯 Concept Used

Friend Function and Non-Member Operator Overloading

💡 Key Point

A friend function can access the private members of a class while remaining a non-member function.
